The compression pipeline is a tightly coupled, event‑driven workflow that sits between the model runtime and the persistent store. It is responsible for (1) extracting low‑rank factors from freshly produced KV pairs, (2) quantizing those factors, (3) persisting the compressed representation, and (4) restoring the original tensors when the model needs to resume a long‑context session. The pipeline is orchestrated by a lightweight Spring Boot microservice that exposes a single REST endpoint, while the heavy lifting is delegated to a Resilience4j‑protected command bus (Axon) and a Kafka event stream that triggers asynchronous compression jobs.

